// Every product e_A e_B of two blades of five diagonal signatures, computed
// by multiplying published matrices: R(0, 1, 0) with e1 the quaternion i =
// [[i, 0], [0, -i]], the complex numbers; R(0, 2, 0) with e1 and e2 the
// quaternions i and j = [[0, 1], [-1, 0]] of the complex 2 x 2
// representation, so e12 is k; R(1, 1, 0) with e1 and e2 the
// split-quaternions j = [[0, 1], [1, 0]] and i = [[0, 1], [-1, 0]], the real
// 2 x 2 matrices, so e12 is -k; R(3, 0, 0) with e1, e2, e3 the Pauli
// matrices; and R(1, 3, 0) with e1 to e4 the Dirac matrices gamma^0 to
// gamma^3 in the Dirac basis, with eta of signature (+ - - -). A blade is
// the product of its generators' matrices in increasing order. Each set of
// matrices was checked to satisfy e_i e_j + e_j e_i = 2 g_ij and to be
// faithful: its 2^n blade matrices are linearly independent over the reals.
// Each table equals the one clifford_reference.py computes with no matrices.
// Products are listed in order of a, then b.
// Fact: e_i e_j + e_j e_i = 2 g_ij
